    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0139" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 3/65: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-18T01:00:00-05:00">December 18, 1941—1
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>673. Minister of Foreign Relations<anchor n="23" xml:id="d169-f1"/> told me that
                    speaking purely personally, since he had no right to speak officially, the
                    Peruvian Ambassador had been continuously making representations that his
                    country’s differences with Ecuador should under no circumstances even be
                    referred to in the forthcoming consultative conference. On the other hand
                    Ecuador had been insisting although unofficially that there should be
                    discussion.</p>
                <p>The Minister felt it was best for this matter not to arise in the conference but
                    that recognition of its existence should be taken outside of the conference as
                    for instance by a statement to be made by the mediating nations giving
                    assurances that the affair was well in hand.</p>
                <pb facs="0140" n="130" xml:id="pg130"/>
                <p>I said I would transmit his thoughts to the Department and he earnestly requested
                    that I do so.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
